Ladybird reports MacIntel on macOS, Win32 on Windows, iPhone on iOS,
and the kernel’s name and machine elsewhere. Blink’s
NavigatorID::platform() returns "MacIntel" on Mac and "Win32" on
Windows, and uname()’s sysname and machine on other systems. WebKit’s
NavigatorBase::platform() does the same, with PAL::deviceName() on
iOS. Gecko’s Navigator::GetPlatform() always answers "MacIntel" on
macOS, even on ARM64, and takes nsHttpHandler’s mPlatform elsewhere.
